# Terms and Conditions

## Intended Use

P1 compute clusters are primarily for research projects. Commercial use is generally not
permitted on the P1 DTU and NGC HPCs; however, Gefion may accommodate certain commercial research
projects on a case-by-case basis.

## Resource Policy

Resources are limited and prioritised for P1 members at the PhD, postdoc, and faculty levels. We
are committed to open access and strive to serve as many P1 members as possible. For very
large-scale projects, we encourage you to reach out to discuss potential solutions.

## Access and Responsibility

P1 does not directly operate the compute resources, as these are managed by the respective
institutions. However, P1 provides guidance and support for using these resources and works
closely with the institutions to ensure they meet the needs of P1-affiliated researchers.

### Access Eligibility

P1 HPC resources are intended for academic research purposes only and are available exclusively
to researchers at Danish universities. Industry access is generally prohibited unless it is part
of a research collaboration with a Danish university.

If you are not affiliated with a Danish university but are working on a project with a
university-affiliated researcher, we can create an additional guest agreement covering data
privacy and security to grant you access to these resources.

## User Revision Policy

User review happens once or twice a year. We cannot rely on personal email addresses for this
process, so we use emails managed by partner institutions to verify user activity.

During each review, users receive an email asking them to:

- Confirm they are still actively using the cluster (no response may indicate that the partner university has revoked access)
- Provide a brief explanation of their current research activities

The HPC governance board receives a list of all current accounts so they can step in for manual
review if needed.

Users who either fail to respond or are not approved by the governance board will have their
account placed in a 6-month grace period.

## Data Retention Policy

Once an account enters the grace period, the user's data is moved to a temporary storage
location, where it will remain for the duration of the grace period (6 months, until the next
review cycle). This allows for recovery or changes in data ownership. The user can at any time
request to have their data deleted.

**Data Recovery Process:**

- Users can request data recovery during the grace period by contacting the HPC governance board
- Data ownership can be transferred to another approved user during this time
- After the grace period ends, all data in temporary storage will be permanently deleted

**Important:** Users should ensure they have backed up any important data before or during the
grace period, as data recovery after the grace period is not possible.

## Detailed Cluster Information

Each cluster is hosted at a separate institution and managed by its own administrators. This site
provides an overview and a starting point for accessing P1 compute resources. For the most
up-to-date technical details, refer to the respective cluster websites and support channels — the
per-cluster pages in this documentation list each provider's docs.

